test: Do not clean up after the tests that run -*notify commands

On Windows, a -*notify child process inherits the node's standard output
and standard error, which the functional test framework redirects to
files in the test directory. bitcoind does not wait for such a child,
so one that outlives it keeps those files open, and the framework's
cleanup of the test directory fails with WinError 32 although every
test case passed.

Pass --nocleanup to the three tests that make the node run a shell
command, so that they leave their test directories behind.

The hunks carry no context lines, as the test list changes often. Apply
with `git apply --unidiff-zero`.

Temporary until https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/28529 is
resolved upstream.

Applied by the Windows workflows that run the functional tests.

